Chapter: PlugBuildScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit
  cites Build chapter PlugBuildPipeline

 We say:

 THE ENTRY CHAPTER ONLY. Everything a reader or a test wants is in
 `PlugBuildPipeline` beside this, because a chapter that declares `opening` can be
 cited by nothing (CDX3001, L-UNCITABLE) and the pipeline of every generator was
 therefore unreachable. This half is the thin entry over the citable rest, the
 same repair `DbBootMain` and `EntryPoint.codex` made.

 THE DRIFT GATE FOLLOWS THIS CHAPTER'S CITES to find the pipeline. It used to read
 `sh-script` or `pl-name` out of the generator's own text, and a generator matching
 neither is not reported as broken, it is not reported at all, so a split like this
 one would have dropped out of the gate silently. That hazard is named in the
 gate's own comment and is why the discovery had to change in the same changelist
 as the split.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell pb-pipe))
  end

